<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112049" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φον-ή</span></b> , ἡ, always, exc.
		in <i><span class="en">
			Suid.
		</span></i>, in pl., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>carnage,</i>
			esp. on the field of battle, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσπαίροντας ἐν ἀργαλέῃσι φονῇσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.521
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν φοναῖς καλῶς πεσόντ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					447
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν φοναῖς πεπτῶτ᾽ ἄθαπτον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					696
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτι ἐν τῇσι φονῇσι ἐόντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					9.76
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κομισθέντα ἐκ τῶν φονῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					5.1
				</span></i>
			; also of slain beasts, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηρὶ μαχέσσασθαι ἕλικος βοὸς ἀμφὶ
					φονῇσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.633
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν φοναῖς θηροκτόνοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					154
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>blood shed by slaying,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῆκέ τ᾽ Αἴγισθον ἐν φοναῖς</span>
			laid him weltering <i>in his blood,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				11.37
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				1.18
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				3.21
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φονῶν</span> is prob. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόνων</span> in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tr.</u>
				558
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑρπετὰ καὶ δάκετα . . ὑπ᾽
				ἐμᾶς πτέρυγος ἐν φοναῖς ὄλλυται</span> come to a
				<i>bloody</i> end, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1070
			</span></i> (lyr., paratrag.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποίῳ δὲ
				κἀπελύσατ᾽ ἐν φοναῖς τρόπῳ;</span> what was the manner
			of her <i>bloody</i> end? <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1314
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοναῖς</span>
			<i>murderously,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1003
			</span></i> (expld. as Adj. by Sch., cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φονός</span>).</div>
